# Sitemap and new routes

Google Search Console only needs a valid `sitemap.xml` at your live origin (e.g. `https://ajzichella.com/sitemap.xml`). This project serves it from [public/sitemap.xml](public/sitemap.xml), which Vite copies into `dist` on build—no extra build step required.

When you add a **new indexable** `<Route path="...">` in [src/App.tsx](src/App.tsx):

1. Add a `<url>` entry in [public/sitemap.xml](public/sitemap.xml) with full `https://ajzichella.com` + pathname and an updated `<lastmod>` (ISO date `YYYY-MM-DD`).
2. Do **not** add URLs that are only redirects (e.g. `/portfolio` → `/case-studies`) or duplicate the home catch-all (`*`).

If you edit the route table, verify the sitemap list still matches every public page you want indexed.

Prerendered static HTML (ATS/crawlers) is generated for every sitemap route **except** `/case-studies/ddos-protection` (password-gated; uses `dist/404.html` SPA shell). Update [scripts/sitemap-routes.mjs](scripts/sitemap-routes.mjs) when adding routes.

Agent-readable plain-text files live in [public/resume.txt](public/resume.txt) and [public/llms.txt](public/llms.txt); keep them updated when experience or case studies change.
